<h2 id="description" data-id="Description">Description</h2>
<p><strong>Basic v2.7</strong> is a cost-effective IoT entry-level main controller. It uses the Espressif <strong>ESP32</strong> chip, equipped with 2 low-power <strong>Xtensa® 32-bit LX6</strong> microprocessors, with a main frequency of up to <strong>240 MHz</strong>. It has onboard <strong>16 MB FLASH</strong> memory, integrated with a <strong>2.0-inch full-color high-definition IPS display panel</strong>, <strong>speaker</strong>, <strong>TFCard slot</strong>, and other peripherals. The full-cover casing ensures the <strong>stability</strong> of circuit operation even in complex industrial application scenarios. The internal bus provides multiple common interface resources (ADC/DAC/I2C/UART/SPI, etc.), with 15 x IO leads on the bottom bus, offering strong expandability. It is suitable for various product prototype development, industrial control, and smart building application scenarios.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0056/7689/2250/files/1920x600-1_0764cfe8-8418-4e2d-b93f-dcef77fcfe51.webp?v=1766822714" alt=""></p>
